c6=A.a(["A proportion observed in a sample (p\u0302 = x/n) estimates an unknown proportion in the population. The 95% confidence interval (CI) gathers the population values compatible with the data, under the assumptions of the calculation.",'"95%" describes the method: repeated over many samples, it would produce intervals containing the true value 95% of the time. For ONE given interval, we do not say it has a 95% chance of containing the true value.',"The Wald CI (p\u0302 \xb1 1.96\u221a(p\u0302(1\u2212p\u0302)/n)) performs poorly when p\u0302 is close to 0 or 1 or when n is small. Prefer the Wilson CI or the exact Clopper-Pearson CI.",'With zero events, the true proportion is not zero: the "rule of three" gives a one-sided 95% upper bound \u2248 3/n.'],c5)
