e9=A.a(["Se = proportion of positive tests among the diseased; Sp = proportion of negative tests among the non-diseased. They describe the test (in a given patient spectrum).","PPV and NPV depend on prevalence: the same test has a low PPV when the disease is rare.","Likelihood ratios (LR+ = Se/(1\u2212Sp), LR\u2212 = (1\u2212Se)/Sp) convert a pre-test probability into a post-test probability.","Case-control recruitment (severe patients versus healthy volunteers) overestimates Se and Sp (spectrum bias) and makes PPV/NPV non-transferable.","To combine several studies, the bivariate model analyses Se and Sp together: they are correlated across studies (different thresholds, threshold effect). The SROC curve and the prediction region show the variability expected from one setting to another."],c5)
