f5=A.a(["Quantitative outcome, two independent groups: t-test. Welch's test does not assume equal variances and loses very little when they are equal: a good default choice.","Small, highly skewed samples or ordinal outcome: Mann-Whitney, which compares distributions (not specifically medians).","More than two groups: ANOVA (or Welch); Kruskal-Wallis for an ordinal outcome. The global test does not say which groups differ: pairwise comparisons (Tukey, Games-Howell if variances differ, Dunn after Kruskal-Wallis) do so while controlling the family-wise error rate; if not planned, they remain exploratory.","Always report the effect size (difference in means, CI) and not only p."],c5)
