i8=A.a(["Q tests for heterogeneity (low power with few studies). I\xb2 estimates the share of variability due to true differences between studies; \u03c4\xb2 gives its variance on the effect scale.","With random effects, the CI concerns the MEAN effect. The prediction interval shows where the effect would lie in a new comparable study.","High I\xb2: look for explanations planned a priori (population, dose, risk of bias); sometimes, do not pool.","Before any pooling, check that the studies answer the same question (PICO, follow-up, measure).","Meta-regression relates the effect to a study characteristic (latitude, dose, year): it explores heterogeneity but remains observational and aggregated (ecological bias); its moderators must be planned a priori."],c5)
