B.b7Q=s(["comparer les patients qui l'ont re\xe7u un jour aux autres","exclure les patients d\xe9c\xe9d\xe9s avant d'avoir pu le recevoir","le coder en covariable d\xe9pendant du temps (ou faire une analyse \xab landmark \xbb)"],t.s)
B.adp=new A.aS("Pour estimer l'effet d'un traitement commenc\xe9 en cours de suivi, il faut\u2026",B.b7Q,2,null,0,"Les deux premi\xe8res options cr\xe9ent ou aggravent le biais du temps immortel.")
B.adr=new A.aS("Same example: cumulative incidence of relapse at month 2, in %?",B.M,-1,10,0.01,"Aalen-Johansen: S(1) \xd7 10/90 = 0.90 \xd7 0.111 = 10%.")
B.adt=new A.aS("100 patients, no censoring. Month 1: 10 die without relapse. Month 2: 10 relapse. Naive 1 \u2212 Kaplan-Meier for relapse at month 2, in % (two decimals)?",B.M,-1,11.11,0.006,"Deaths treated as censoring: 1 \u2212 (1 \u2212 10/90) = 11.11%. The cumulative incidence is 10/100 = 10%: the naive estimate overestimates it.")
B.adu=new A.aS("N = 20 000, h\xb2 = 0,25, score LD moyen 80, M = 1 000 000 de variants, sans confusion. \u03c7\xb2 moyen attendu (deux d\xe9cimales) ?",B.M,-1,1.4,0.006,"1 + N\xb7h\xb2\xb7\u2113\u0304/M = 1 + 20 000 \xd7 0,25 \xd7 80 / 1 000 000 = 1,40 : un \u03bb nettement sup\xe9rieur \xe0 1 sans aucune confusion.")
B.b4p=s(["use OR = 1.6","assume a smaller OR: the effects reported at discovery are overestimated (winner's curse)","use \u03b1 = 0.05 for the replication of all variants"],t.s)
B.adx=new A.aS("A first GWAS reports OR = 1.6 for a variant. To plan the replication, we should\u2026",B.b4p,1,null,0,"Discovery selects the estimates that happen to be largest; the true effect is generally smaller.")
B.ady=new A.aS("Schoenfeld: number of events to detect HR = 0.5 with 80% power, \u03b1 = 0.05, 1:1 allocation (nearest integer)?",B.M,-1,65,1,"d = (1.96 + 0.84)\xb2 \xd7 4 / (log 0.5)\xb2 = 7.85 \xd7 4 / 0.480 \u2248 65 events.")
B.adz=new A.aS("\u03b2X = 0.05 with a standard error of 0.01. F statistic of this instrument?",B.M,-1,25,0.5,"F \u2248 (\u03b2X/se)\xb2 = 5\xb2 = 25 \u2265 10: instrument strong enough.")
B.biv=s(["Le RR","La diff\xe9rence de risques","L'OR"],t.s)
B.adA=new A.aS("Dans une \xe9tude cas-t\xe9moins, quelle mesure est estimable ?",B.biv,2,null,0,"Les cas et t\xe9moins sont \xe9chantillonn\xe9s sur l'issue : les risques ne sont pas estimables.")
B.bj6=s(["One of the two models is wrong","Age speeds up relapse among those still alive, but older patients die before relapsing, so the share who relapse does not increase","Age has no effect"],t.s)
B.adB=new A.aS("Age: cause-specific HR of relapse 1.03 per year, sHR 0.99. Interpretation?",B.bj6,1,null,0,"Both are correct: they answer two different questions.")
B.adC=new A.aS("Schoenfeld : nombre d'\xe9v\xe9nements pour d\xe9tecter HR = 0,5 avec 80 % de puissance, \u03b1 = 0,05, allocation 1:1 (entier le plus proche) ?",B.M,-1,65,1,"d = (1,96 + 0,84)\xb2 \xd7 4 / (log 0,5)\xb2 = 7,85 \xd7 4 / 0,480 \u2248 65 \xe9v\xe9nements.")
B.bda=s(["all instruments are valid","at least half of the weight comes from valid instruments","the MR-Egger intercept is zero"],t.s)
B.adD=new A.aS("The weighted median remains valid if\u2026",B.bda,1,null,0,"The median tolerates up to 50% of the weight from invalid instruments.")
B.b77=s(["Many true associations","Systematic inflation: stratification, relatedness or genotyping problem","Insufficient power"],t.s)
B.adF=new A.aS("On the QQ plot, the points leave the diagonal from the smallest values of \u2212log10 p. Interpretation?",B.b77,1,null,0,"A departure from the start of the plot reflects inflation of all statistics, not isolated signals.")
B.b5u=s(["Doublon d'\xe9chantillon","Parent\u2013enfant","Fr\xe8res/s\u0153urs","Cousins germains"],t.s)
B.adG=new A.aS("Une paire de sujets a \u03c6 = 0,25 et IBS0 \u2248 0. Relation la plus probable ?",B.b5u,1,null,0,"\u03c6 \u2248 0,25 est le 1er degr\xe9 ; IBS0 \u2248 0 (jamais d'homozygotes oppos\xe9s) caract\xe9rise le lien parent\u2013enfant.")
B.b67=s(["Conclude that the variant is under natural selection.","Check the genotyping (calling errors, contamination) before any analysis.","Remove the controls in disequilibrium."],t.s)
B.adH=new A.aS("In controls, a variant departs strongly from Hardy-Weinberg (p = 10\u207b\u2077). First reaction?",B.b67,1,null,0,"In controls, a marked HWE departure is primarily a quality signal.")
B.bf7=s(["Le risque d'infection est nul.","Le risque est compatible avec des valeurs allant jusqu'\xe0 environ 2 %.","L'IC \xe0 95 % est de 0 % \xe0 0 %."],t.s)
B.adI=new A.aS("Aucun cas d'infection sur 150 nouveau-n\xe9s. Quelle formulation est correcte ?",B.bf7,1,null,0,"Z\xe9ro observ\xe9 n'est pas z\xe9ro vrai : 3/150 = 2 % (r\xe8gle de trois).")
B.bi3=s(["Le traitement n'a pas d'effet.","Les donn\xe9es ne permettent pas de conclure : un effet b\xe9n\xe9fique comme d\xe9l\xe9t\xe8re reste compatible.","Il y a 30 % de chances que le traitement soit inefficace."],t.s)
B.adJ=new A.aS("Un essai trouve p = 0,30 et un IC du RR de 0,6 \xe0 1,9. Quelle conclusion ?",B.bi3,1,null,0,"IC large incluant des effets importants dans les deux sens : absence de preuve.")
B.bf4=s(["Un des deux mod\xe8les est faux","L'\xe2ge acc\xe9l\xe8re la rechute chez les patients encore vivants, mais les patients \xe2g\xe9s meurent avant de rechuter : la proportion de rechutes n'augmente pas","L'\xe2ge n'a aucun effet"],t.s)
B.adK=new A.aS("\xc2ge : HR sp\xe9cifique de cause de la rechute 1,03 par an, sHR 0,99. Interpr\xe9tation ?",B.bf4,1,null,0,"Les deux sont justes : ils r\xe9pondent \xe0 deux questions diff\xe9rentes.")
B.beS=s(["excluded from the analysis.","counted as dead at month 14.","included as censored at month 14."],t.s)
B.adL=new A.aS("A patient lost to follow-up at month 14, alive at the last visit, should be\u2026",B.beS,2,null,0,'Censoring keeps the information "alive for at least 14 months".')
B.bdj=s(["the probability that H0 is true is 3%.","if H0 and the model were true, data at least as extreme would be observed 3% of the time.","there is a 97% chance that the effect is real."],t.s)
B.adM=new A.aS("p = 0.03 means that\u2026",B.bdj,1,null,0,"Frequentist definition; the other two answers are classic errors.")
B.adN=new A.aS("Un variant augmente le LDL-cholest\xe9rol de 0,10 mmol/L par all\xe8le (\u03b2X) et le log-odds de maladie coronarienne de 0,03 (\u03b2Y). Estimation de Wald de l'effet causal par mmol/L, en log-odds (deux d\xe9cimales) ?",B.M,-1,0.3,0.006,"\u03b2Y/\u03b2X = 0,03/0,10 = 0,30 log-odds par mmol/L, soit un OR de e^0,30 \u2248 1,35 par mmol/L.")
B.adO=new A.aS("Genome-wide threshold 5 \xd7 10\u207b\u2078: what is its \u2212log10 (two decimals)?",B.M,-1,7.3,0.006,"\u2212log10(5 \xd7 10\u207b\u2078) = 7.30: the red line of a Manhattan plot.")
B.bhq=s(["Il n'a aucun effet","Il est associ\xe9 \xe0 la maladie","Signal suggestif : ni exclu ni d\xe9montr\xe9 ; \xe0 r\xe9pliquer dans une cohorte ind\xe9pendante"],t.s)
B.adP=new A.aS("Un variant a p = 5,8 \xd7 10\u207b\u2075 apr\xe8s ajustement. Quelle conclusion ?",B.bhq,2,null,0,"Le seuil de 5 \xd7 10\u207b\u2078 n'est pas atteint : absence de preuve, pas preuve d'absence (dans la d\xe9monstration 5, c'est un vrai variant causal qui manque de puissance).")
B.bia=s(["Diabetes causes coronary disease","The two diseases share part of their genetic factors","The same patients have both diseases"],t.s)
B.adQ=new A.aS("rg = 0.6 between type 2 diabetes and coronary disease. Conclusion?",B.bia,1,null,0,"rg measures shared genetic effects (pleiotropy or common pathway), not causality; Mendelian randomization addresses causality.")
B.adT=new A.aS("On teste 20 variants ind\xe9pendants sans effet r\xe9el, chacun \xe0 5 %. Combien de faux positifs en moyenne ?",B.M,-1,1,0.01,"20 \xd7 0,05 = 1. D'o\xf9 la n\xe9cessit\xe9 d'une correction des tests multiples.")
B.adU=new A.aS("N = 20,000, h\xb2 = 0.25, mean LD score 80, M = 1,000,000 variants, no confounding. Expected mean \u03c7\xb2 (two decimals)?",B.M,-1,1.4,0.006,"1 + N\xb7h\xb2\xb7\u2113\u0304/M = 1 + 20,000 \xd7 0.25 \xd7 80 / 1,000,000 = 1.40: a \u03bb well above 1 without any confounding.")
B.bhi=s(["The RR","The risk difference","The OR"],t.s)
B.adV=new A.aS("In a case-control study, which measure is estimable?",B.bhi,2,null,0,"Cases and controls are sampled on the outcome: risks are not estimable.")
